 "plan": {
  "angle": "The query has 10 searches a month and no top 10 in the workbook; the people typing it run a mentoring program and need the form itself, not a printable sheet. This page shows the mentorship application form as a working intake: four programs (alumni, a professional society, a startup studio, an internal company program), each with the fields it asks, the rule that reads the answer, and the email that follows, from a scored goal statement to a manager's approval.",
  "tab_stories": [
   "Ashgrove University's alumni mentoring program asks students for graduation year, target industry, and a 150-word goal statement; coordinator Wendeline Strand scores Kofi Abernathy's statement a 4, and any score of 4 or 5 sends an interview invitation by email.",
   "Kestrel Bay Society of Accountants asks mentor applicants for current role, years in practice, and the topics they can mentor on; 5 or more years puts an applicant in the mentor pool, so Rufus Delacroix with 11 years joins it and Imogen Thackeray with 3 years gets an email offering the peer mentor track.",
   "Tallowmere Startup Studio's founder application asks for monthly revenue only when the founder picks the revenue stage; Pebblework reports $18,500 a month, over the $10,000 line, so program director Odile Fairweather gets an email to book a call.",
   "At Larchmont Freight Software, an employee's mentorship application names their manager, who gets an approval email; after 3 days with no reply, the app sends Priscilla Vantongeren a reminder about Desmond Oyelaran's application."
  ],
  "openers": [
   "Ashgrove University pairs students with alumni every fall",
   "Kestrel Bay Society of Accountants runs two mentoring tracks",
   "Tallowmere Startup Studio takes founders at any stage",
   "Nobody at Larchmont Freight Software joins mentoring without a manager's yes",
   "Decide who fills in the form",
   "Ask only for what a match depends on",
   "Cap the goal statement at 150 words",
   "Write the scoring rubric before the first application arrives",
   "Describe the form to Emergent in plain English",
   "Choose who hears about each application",
   "Submit two test applications"
  ],
  "heading_shapes": [
   "Kofi's score of 4 brings an interview invitation",
   "Three years in practice puts Imogen on the peer track",
   "Pebblework's $18,500 month reaches Odile by email",
   "No reply in 3 days, so Priscilla gets a reminder"
  ],
